kings.","published":"2026-11-18T04:34:25.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50514170/cfp-2026-third-committee-top-25-bracket","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Wake Forest surges into CFP top 12; top 4 unchanged while Texas jumps Notre Dame","description":"Alabama stayed at No. 3 despite some struggles on Saturday while two-loss Texas jumped one-loss Notre Dame for No. 5 in the CFP's latest rankings.","published":"2026-11-18T04:55:09.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50515993/wake-forest-surges-cfp-top-12-texas-jumps-notre-dame","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Mark Schlabach","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Pawn shop fighting 'Gold Digger' trademark filed by Jordon Hudson's company","description":"A California pawn shop is opposing a trademark application for \"Gold Digger\" filed by a company connected to Jordan Hudson, then-companion of Bill Belichick.","published":"2026-11-18T00:07:30.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/espn/story/_/id/50514442/pawn-shop-fights-gold-digger-trademark-filed-hudson","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Anthony Olivieri","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Oklahoma coach Venables shouts out Love's after Buc-ee's comment","description":"Venables showed love Sunday to Buc-ee's -- which is owned by an alumnus of the Sooners' next opponent, Texas A&M. So on Tuesday the coach repped the Oklahoma-based Love's.","published":"2026-11-17T22:23:36.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50513199/oklahoma-brent-venables-loves-travel-stop","type":"Story","byline":"J.J. Post","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"2026 college football coaching carousel: Tracking every open job","description":"As the carousel spins, we'll keep you updated with all the comings and goings.","published":"2026-11-17T21:26:31.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50358611/2026-cfb-coaching-carousel-firings-hirings","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"North Texas QB Tayven Jackson out with upper-body injury","description":"North Texas senior quarterback Tayven Jackson, who is sixth in the FBS with 3,005 passing yards, will miss at least the next two games with an upper-body injury.","published":"2026-11-17T20:53:17.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50513204/north-texas-qb-tayven-jackson-upper-body-injury","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Defiant Dabo Swinney says Clemson's 'gonna win a bunch more'","description":"Despite going through a self-described \"rough patch\" over the past two seasons, Clemson coach Dabo Swinney is resolute in his belief that he and the Tigers have a lot more wins ahead of them.","published":"2026-11-17T20:37:09.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50512833/defiant-dabo-swinney-says-clemson-gonna-win-bunch-more","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Andrea Adelson","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5120968/christian-alliegro","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christian_Alliegro"},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Christian Alliegro","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Christian_Alliegro","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-14T07:37:31Z","intro":"Christian Alliegro is an American football linebacker for the Ohio State Buckeyes. He previously played for the Wisconsin Badgers.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Alliegro attended Avon Old Farms School in Avon, Connecticut, and Darien High School in Darien, Connecticut where he was both a football and lacrosse standout, and initially committed to play college lacrosse for the Navy Midshipmen. However, he decided to forgo lacrosse and signed to play college football for the Wisconsin Badgers."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"WISCONSIN\nAs a freshman in 2023, Alliegro played in all 13 games, recording five tackles and a sack. In week 10 of the 2024 season, Alliegro notched 16 tackles in a loss to Iowa. In week 12, he tallied ten tackles in a loss to top-ranked Oregon. Alliegro finished the 2024 season with 66 tackles with five being for a loss and three sacks. In week 9 of the 2025 season, he broke his arm in a loss to Ohio State, but continued playing, posting six tackles with two being for a loss. Alliegro finished the 2025 season with 53 tackles with eight going for a loss and four sacks. After the conclusion of the season, he entered the NCAA transfer portal.\n\nOHIO STATE\nAlliegro transferred to play for the Ohio State Buckeyes."}]}}